      "explanation": "Front Door (with WAF) sends users to the nearest healthy region and fails over on its own. Each region runs a zone-redundant App Service plan with several instances; Azure SQL is zone-redundant with a failover group to the other region. Apps read secrets from a regional Key Vault with a managed identity, data services are reached only through private endpoints, and everything sends diagnostics to Log Analytics. Single-region App Service + SQL is about 99.94%; two regions behind Front Door gets to about 99.99%."
